# Controllers — Orquestradores Puros

Controllers **apenas orquestram**: recebem o request validado → chamam o service/action → retornam o resource. Nunca processam, nunca decidem, nunca persistem.

## Estrutura Obrigatória

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Http\Controllers;

use App\DTOs\Order\CreateOrderDTO;
use App\DTOs\Order\UpdateOrderDTO;
use App\Http\Requests\Order\StoreOrderRequest;
use App\Http\Requests\Order\UpdateOrderRequest;
use App\Http\Resources\Order\OrderCollection;
use App\Http\Resources\Order\OrderResource;
use App\Services\OrderService;
use Illuminate\Http\Response;

final class OrderController extends Controller
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly OrderService $orderService,
    ) {}

    public function index(): OrderCollection
    {
        return new OrderCollection(
            $this->orderService->paginate(),
        );
    }

    public function store(StoreOrderRequest $request): OrderResource
    {
        $order = $this->orderService->create(
            CreateOrderDTO::fromRequest($request),
        );

        return new OrderResource($order);
    }

    public function show(int $id): OrderResource
    {
        return new OrderResource(
            $this->orderService->findOrFail($id),
        );
    }

    public function update(UpdateOrderRequest $request, int $id): OrderResource
    {
        $order = $this->orderService->update(
            $id,
            UpdateOrderDTO::fromRequest($request),
        );

        return new OrderResource($order);
    }

    public function destroy(int $id): Response
    {
        $this->orderService->delete($id);

        return response()->noContent();
    }
}
```

## Regras

- Classe `final` — sem herança de controllers
- Dependências injetadas via construtor com `readonly`
- Sempre use `$request->validated()` — nunca `$request->all()` ou `$request->input()`
- Passe **DTOs** ao service, nunca arrays crus
- Retorne sempre `Resource`, `ResourceCollection` ou `response()->noContent()`
- Zero lógica de negócio, zero queries, zero condicionais de domínio
- Zero try/catch — exceções são tratadas pelo Handler global

## Anti-Patterns

```php
// ❌ Validação no controller
public function store(Request $request): JsonResponse {
    $request->validate([...]);
}

// ❌ Array cru para o service
$this->orderService->create($request->validated());

// ❌ Lógica de negócio no controller
$order = Order::create([...]);
Mail::send(...);
$order->total = $order->items->sum('price');

// ❌ Retornar model direto
return response()->json($order);

// ❌ try/catch no controller
try {
    $order = Order::findOrFail($id);
} catch (ModelNotFoundException $e) {
    return response()->json(['message' => 'Not found'], 404);
}

// ❌ Query direta no controller
$orders = Order::where('status', 'pending')->get();
```
